# Shell scripts and unit files run on Linux, and are edited on Windows.
#
# git's autocrlf turned run-eval.sh into CRLF on checkout, and dash reads
# "set -eu\r" as an illegal option. The script died on line 13 with a message
# that says nothing about line endings. These files are LF wherever they live.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.service text eol=lf
*.timer text eol=lf
Dockerfile* text eol=lf
*.conf text eol=lf

# Python is read by the interpreter, which does not care, but the containers
# do run it on Linux and a stray CR in a heredoc has bitten before.
*.py text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
